      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f319e833bb16b63456b2cd7|full_name}: Yes your logic is sound in isolation of the feature itself. However, there are multiple reasons as to why you might be seeing that behaviour. Your logic relies mostly on experience, or time played, without considering why it takes that time for users to start complaining about the limitations of the feature. If for some miracle the lack of understanding was not a part or the cause of the issue with lower ranks, I still presented the comments regarding the arbitrary limits.\nThe initial 2 sections, while certainly focused on this canny request to keep my comment relevant to this feedback, were indeed an annoyance at those that continually attempt to justify tiering features between the ranks. I apologise if you found personal offence in my initial comments.\nYes you have a solid request with a well outlined idea, no we should not be giving more to higher ranks, especially in a social game,  and I will continue to downvote any request that promotes the rank system by justifying changes within the system that shifts power or access to features where unnecessary or harmful.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
